iles and/or minimum and maximum values and estimated the mean and SD using the Box-Cox method, which does not rely on the assumption of normality [ 13 ]. We used the website graphic user interface [ 13 ]. When a study reported results separately by subgroups (other than cases-controls and respiratory diseases), we combined them into a single group [ 14 ]. The standardized mean and confidence interval ( \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
